tion probability to be non-negligibly close to 1, by using an
all-or-nothing transform

\begin{quote}
(see {[}33{]}). We also assume that the decoder \emph{D} is
stateless/resettable, i.e., it cannot see and adapt to it being tested
and replies independently to successive queries. Handling

stateful pirate boxes has been investigated in {[}31, 30{]}.

In our scheme, algorithm Trace will only be a conrmation algorithm. It
takes as

input a set of (suspect) users (\emph{Uij})\emph{j} of cardinality
\emph{k ≤t}, and must satisfy the following two properties:

\emph{•} Confirmation. If the traitors are all in the set of suspects
(\emph{Uij})\emph{j≤k}, then it returns User \emph{Uij}0 is guilty for
some \emph{j}0 \emph{≤k};\\
\emph{•} Soundness. If it returns User \emph{Uij}0 is guilty for some
\emph{j}0 \emph{≤k}, then user \emph{Uij}0 should indeed be a traitor.
\end{quote}

The conrmation algorithm should run in polynomial-time. It may be
converted into a

(costly) full-edge tracing algorithm by calling it on all subsets of
users of cardinality \emph{t}.

7

